{"items":[{"path":"tools.hold_arm","description":"Coordinator only. Arm a hold pair from a HOOK SET verdict: both plans stop before their named phase's implementer starts. Both plans must be linked, each phase must be in its status table and not done, and a plan whose overlapping work is already implemented leads. Returns every armed hold.","signature":"tools.hold_arm({
  first: {
    /** Plan name: its branch and its folder under AGENT-INSTRUCTIONS/PLANS/. */
    plan: string,
    /** Id of the phase, from the plan's status table, whose implementer may not start yet. */
    phase: string,
  },
  second: {
    /** Plan name: its branch and its folder under AGENT-INSTRUCTIONS/PLANS/. */
    plan: string,
    /** Id of the phase, from the plan's status table, whose implementer may not start yet. */
    phase: string,
  },
  /** The leading plan, one of the two. */
  leading: string,
  /** The verdict's reason, shown to both orchestrators. */
  reason: string,
}): Promise<string | null>"}],"remaining":0,"next":null}

input.code:
return await tools.hold_arm({
  first: { plan: "plan-a", phase: "A1" },
  second: { plan: "plan-b", phase: "B1" },
  leading: "plan-b",
  reason: "Both active phases rewrite the same `HitRecord` struct in `src/hittable.rs` (A1 adds the material field; B1 adds `front_face`, `u`, `v` and a `HitRecord::new` constructor that flips the normal against the ray) and the same single construction site in `Sphere::hit` in `src/sphere.rs`. B1 also redefines what `normal` means, while A2 is specified to tell entering from leaving by the outward normal already on the record, so merging the branches blindly would leave the material/glass contract wrong; the merge needs one agreed shape.",
});

return await tools.hold_arm({
  first: { plan: "plan-a", phase: "A1" },
  second: { plan: "plan-c", phase: "C3" },
  leading: "plan-c",
  reason: "plan-c's committed C1 already rewrote `src/main.rs` — `render` now takes `samples` with a per-pixel averaging loop calling `ray_colour(&ray, &world)`, `to_byte` is `pub(crate)`, and the module list/tests changed — while plan-a's A1 is detailed against the old `render(width, height)`, replacing the colour computation with a 50-bounce `Material` loop threaded by one seeded `Rng` and rewriting `ray_colour`, `to_byte` (gamma), the module list and the unit tests in the same hunks. The merge needs a design choice on the combined render signature and loop nesting (sample averaging versus bounce scattering, where the single `Rng` lives, how gamma applies to averaged samples), and C3's progress line lands in that same loop.",
});

return await tools.hold_arm({
  first: { plan: "plan-a", phase: "A1" },
  second: { plan: "plan-b", phase: "B2" },
  leading: "plan-a",
  reason: "Both rewrite the same `scene()` function in `src/main.rs`: A1 gives the two existing spheres materials and adds a metal sphere, while B2 replaces the ground sphere with a `Plane` and adds a `Triangle`, so each branch alone passes but the merged scene must combine the edits and fix how materials attach to the new shapes. A1 also changes `HitRecord` and `HittableList::hit` in `src/hittable.rs`, which B3's `bounding_box` and box test build on, so the overlap returns there.",
});
